From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Will Faust <willtechnoduck@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 23 Sep 2026 03:13:14 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] iOS JIT: retry code-generation sweeps while holders were
 skipped, alias-table capacity diagnostic, pool placement fixes

The once-per-generation sweep marked a generation swept even when it skipped
threads that were in simulation or signal-pinned, so the outgoing 128 MB code
buffer stayed pinned while every successor was refused to 16-32 MB and the
JIT rotated (2.1 M recompiles in 90 s, 400-1000 ms frames). The same
generation is now re-swept every 16th trigger while the last pass skipped
anyone, at most 256 times; the gen-sweep log line reports each pass.

Also: IosAliasEntries logs when it is full and refuses an image; exec-redirect
census records the caller; the 0x140000000 window plug rule only plugs holes
that end below the placeholder and only while the window is held; backpatch
decline logging; self-modifying-write counters; CRT allocation hooks.

Madeira-commit: 89db11f589b29a5ef06d9bc62be9726938dbbda0
Rebased: resolved
Class: madeira-port
Evidence: docs/evidence/2026-09-24-fex-latest-rebase.md
Offered-upstream: no
